    "updated_at": "2022-02-16T13:29:06Z",
    "body": "Treating it like `display: none` would make canvas fallback content not focusable at all. Which would be another possibility, but seems a riskier change. I basically did the minimal change to consistently handle inertness (it's tracked in the computed style, so it's a problem if elements in `display: none` that don't have a cached computed style can be focused).",
